{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"1739 patch set 2 advisories: one was a CORRECTNESS REGRESSION I introduced, and it is worse\nthan the reviewer stated.\n\n## The empty-map path made things worse than before the change\n\n`_sweep_position_map` returned `{}` when the map could not be built (git failure), and\n`_run_sweep` threaded that into every fold. But\n`compact_txn._build_authorship_ledger` rebuilds its own per-ticket map only when the argument\n`is None` (`compact_txn.py:114`). An empty dict is a perfectly valid map that simply misses\nevery lookup — so every event fell through to `resolve_event_commit`, then\n`resolve_position_commit`, PER EVENT, INSIDE the store write lock.\n\nThat is not \"degrading to the old behaviour\". It is the full bug-7084 pathology — per-EVENT\nfull-history walks under the lock, the 6.78s-per-event case — strictly worse than the\nper-ticket walk this whole ticket exists to remove. And my own comment on that line asserted\nthe opposite: \"an empty map simply restores the per-ticket behaviour\". It restores the per-event\nbehaviour.\n\nFixed: `_sweep_position_map` now returns `dict | None` and yields `None` on failure AND on an\nempty result, so each fold rebuilds its own per-ticket map — the honest degradation. Added a\ntest that injects a builder failure and asserts the fallback is per-TICKET (>=1 ticket_map\nbuild) and NOT per-event (0 per_event, 0 per_position). Verified RED against the `{}` version\nwith a counted revert (1 -> 1) rather than a trusted string edit.\n\n## The second advisory was another half-assertion of mine\n\n`test_the_sweep_commit_does_not_steal_a_concurrent_writers_event` asserted only that the stray\nfile was ABSENT from the commit — never that the legitimately folded SNAPSHOT was PRESENT. So\nit would have passed if my scoped `git add -- {tid}/` staged nothing at all, \"fixing\" the theft\nby committing nothing. Added the positive half.\n\n## Also caught by the gates, not by me\n\n`mypy` rejected the change: I updated `_sweep_position_map`'s return type but my edit to\n`_sweep_one_ticket`'s parameter annotation silently did not apply — the target string had been\nreflowed by `ruff format`. Same stale-string trap as the RED-check near-miss earlier today, and\nthe second time in one session that an edit I believed had applied had not. I am now verifying\nreplacement counts rather than trusting `str.replace`, and the typechecker caught what I did\nnot.\n\nGates green after all of it: ruff, mypy 527 files, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0, 39\ntests across the three compaction suites. Amended and pushed BEFORE starting the tiers this\ntime, so nothing races them."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786655425738056001,"uuid":"012284bb-0732-45a9-a2c0-8934f76921bf"}